{"version":"1","id":"rebeloper","handle":"rebeloper","name":"Rebeloper","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--W0sZL8K4--/f_auto/v1726990075/logos/rebeloper","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.4573,"y":-0.4398,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":414,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T17:57:09.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-10-04T13:28:31.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.006039,"listicle_ratio":0.004831,"question_ratio":0.379227,"avg_read_time":1.806763,"summary_length_avg":353.0,"title_length_avg":67.949275,"title_length_var":321.714818,"tag_entropy":3.262461,"tag_diversity":0.217391,"top_tag_share":0.13285,"avg_upvotes":0.05314,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.002415,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.086957,"zero_engagement_share":0.963768,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":4.994966,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":2.833333},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.5588,-6.8088],"cadence_depth":[7.9412,-7.9706],"hype_variety":[-0.7353,0.9412],"title_style":[9.9706,1.1029]},"top_tags":[["swiftui",142],["swift",125],["ios",115],["mobile",50],["data-structures",37],["xcode",31],["testing",23],["cicd",20]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Implementing and Managing View States in SwiftUI","Mobile App A/B Testing - Step-by-step tutorial","Build an animated loading button with multiple states in SwiftUI"],"outlier":["28 April 2026"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"IQ21jiKI4","title":"Looking back, what issue did you hit when DTOs started carrying business logic indirectly?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E3VGeC9txlg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/looking-back-what-issue-did-you-hit-when-dtos-started-carrying-business-logic-indirectly--iq21jiki4","summary":"A brief reflection on the pitfall of letting business logic leak into DTOs through computed flags. When DTO semantics changed, application logic based on those flags produced wrong decisions. The fix was stripping DTOs back to raw data transport and moving all logic into the domain layer.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/E3VGeC9txlg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T17:57:09.000Z"},{"id":"1euQ1cBNO","title":"Why force unwraps in production code are a code review red flag","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ESxsFI8hRCE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/when-reviewing-code-what-optional-misuse-instantly-raises-a-red-flag-for-you--1euq1cbno","summary":"Force unwraps in production code are a common red flag during code review. Trusting upstream API guarantees without enforcement can lead to unexpected crashes on edge cases. The recommended fix is to eliminate force unwraps entirely in production, and when early failure is necessary, fail explicitly with context rather than crashing silently later.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ESxsFI8hRCE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T12:53:38.000Z"},{"id":"u3A8onxUd","title":"You\u2019ve dealt with async pipelines. What broke when DTO decoding happened o\ufb00 the main flow?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MJyDQ4l7Cj4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-ve-dealt-with-async-pipelines-what-broke-when-dto-decoding-happened-o-the-main-flow--u3a8onxud","summary":"When DTO decoding runs off the main flow in async pipelines, mapping can lag behind, causing the UI to render partial data before correcting itself. The root cause is splitting decode and map into separate async steps. The fix is atomic transformation: combining decode and map into a single step so the UI always receives complete, consistent data.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MJyDQ4l7Cj4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T10:46:50.000Z"},{"id":"J011LK65W","title":"Fix SwiftUI stale UI by mapping optionals to explicit state enums","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eF5ibuI9VtM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-ve-debugged-ui-glitches-in-swiftui-did-optionals-play-a-role-there--j011lk65w","summary":"Binding optionals directly into SwiftUI views can cause stale UI without crashes, because SwiftUI struggles to track nil-to-value transitions consistently. The fix is to map optionals into explicit view state enums, making state transitions clear and bugs visible.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/eF5ibuI9VtM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T08:46:11.000Z"},{"id":"5CxFvtfz9","title":"In one of your past iOS systems, what happened when DTOs were reused across multiple endpoints?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zrvq-HJp6F8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/in-one-of-your-past-ios-systems-what-happened-when-dtos-were-reused-across-multiple-endpoints--5cxfvtfz9","summary":"Reusing a single DTO across multiple iOS endpoints caused a screen to display wrong values when one endpoint changed its shape. The fix was splitting DTOs per endpoint, accepting duplication as a safer trade-off since endpoints evolve independently over time.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Zrvq-HJp6F8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T17:15:17.000Z"},{"id":"QS6c5eYgu","title":"Design a Better SwiftUI Button Experience","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dW79JbtDi5c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/design-a-better-swiftui-button-experience-qs6c5eygu","summary":"A tutorial walkthrough covering how to use Swift's async/await syntax in SwiftUI to fetch data from an API, replacing older completion handler and Result-based patterns with a cleaner single-line asynchronous call inside a task with do-catch error handling.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dW79JbtDi5c/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T13:44:38.000Z"},{"id":"xuRY2F8ud","title":"What broke in production when your DTOs drifted from your domain models in large Swift apps?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=svdbkNSdnIo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-broke-in-production-when-your-dtos-drifted-from-your-domain-models-in-large-swift-apps--xury2f8ud","summary":"A cautionary tale about DTO drift in large Swift apps: adding an optional field to a DTO caused silent mapping failures that defaulted to empty states, only surfacing weeks later in production. The fix was strict decoding with fail-fast behavior and treating DTOs as versioned contracts rather than flexible data bags.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/svdbkNSdnIo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T10:50:45.000Z"},{"id":"KeoqnWeiy","title":"How to convert completion handlers to async/await using Swift continuations","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9ssMcvKo0rc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-swiftui-button-instantly-looks-better-keoqnweiy","summary":"A walkthrough of converting completion handler-based APIs to Swift's async/await pattern using continuations. Shows how to wrap an old callback API using `withCheckedThrowingContinuation`, handle success and failure cases with `continuation.resume`, and simplify the switch-on-result pattern using the `resume(with:)` overload that accepts a Result directly.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9ssMcvKo0rc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T05:15:37.000Z"},{"id":"OQm3tj4Jx","title":"SwiftUI Loading Button That Feels Native","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=05XdpMVC-Po","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/swiftui-loading-button-that-feels-native-oqm3tj4jx","summary":"A tutorial walkthrough converting completion-handler-based network calls to Swift's async/await pattern in a SwiftUI context. Covers creating an async throws function to fetch profiles, and using withCheckedThrowingContinuation to bridge existing completion-based APIs to the modern async/await model.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/05XdpMVC-Po/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T18:21:59.000Z"},{"id":"5LwiK9Tf1","title":"In large codebases, where do optionals quietly create long-term damage?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bydtjIUknHE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/in-large-codebases-where-do-optionals-quietly-create-long-term-damage--5lwik9tf1","summary":"In large codebases, optional values that leak beyond the data layer into domain and application layers cause long-term architectural damage. Partial models propagate across layers, forcing defensive null checks everywhere and slowing development velocity. The fix is enforcing fully initialized models past the data layer, keeping optionals only at the edge boundary.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bydtjIUknHE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T16:38:18.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["neciudan","magdamiu","decuberss","laracasts","kotlinwkly"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","kloss_xyz"],"similar":[{"id":"neciudan","handle":"neciudan","name":"Neciu Dan","is_squad":false,"x":-4.4223,"y":-0.2697,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":27,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--xeHLtkTA--/f_auto,q_auto/v1776585705/logos/neciudan","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":14.461037,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.018519,"avg_read_time":13.62963,"tag_diversity":1.555556},"top_tags_preview":[["javascript",10],["react",6],["career",4]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.2353,7.4706],"cadence_depth":[-7.1765,7.75],"hype_variety":[4.4118,2.9265],"title_style":[-6.25,9.9412]}},{"id":"magdamiu","handle":"magdamiu","name":"Magda Miu","is_squad":false,"x":-4.6093,"y":-0.1775,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":11,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/58d2df5ee26844e99f4cf9a5e92e6c09","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.068515,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":9.363636,"tag_di